# The same modem asked for Bell 202, which is not permitted on
# Australian lines, and refused.  So the recording is a modem calling
# and nothing ever answering it in a mode either end can hold.
#
# It earns its place as the second `connect: none` in the corpus, and
# a different kind from the first: `no-v32-answerer` is a far end that
# will not go to V.32, and this is a far end that will not go anywhere.
# What must not happen is a connect -- an automode start-up that ends in
# CONNECT here has locked to something that is not a data signal.
source:    recordings/third-party/netcomm-2400sa-bell202.wav, left channel
seconds:   9.0
role:      originate
modes:     bell103,v21,v22,v22bis
v8:        no
connect:   none
tolerance: 0
